.po 1i
.TH GLOB 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 16:53:52
.\"@[$]glob.1C	1.5	08/15/84 16:53:52 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.fi
.SH NAME
glob \- print strings on the terminal without spaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BR glob " wordlist"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Like
.B echo,
but no \e escapes are recognized and words are delimited
by null characters in the output.
Useful for programs which use the shell to expand a list of words.
.SH SEE ALSO
echo(1C), echo2(1).
.br
.I "The C Shell" 
in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
